SGLang patch on top of the vendored llama.cpp tree (ggml/, see ggml/LLAMA_CPP_COMMIT).
Applied with `patch -p1` to a copy of ggml/ in the build tree (CMakeLists.txt); the
vendored files themselves stay byte-identical to llama.cpp (ggml/SHA256SUMS).

MMQ: write dst as f32, f16 or bf16 (mmq_args::type_dst, default f32).

The kernels accumulate in fp32 as before and round each output once, when it is
stored (round to nearest even), so a f16/bf16 dst holds exactly the f32 result
converted to that type. For the stream-k decomposition, the partial sum of the
block that finishes a tile started by a previous block would otherwise be stored
in dst and the fixup kernel would add the earlier partial sums to the rounded
value; with a half-precision dst that partial sum goes to a second fixup slot of
the block instead, and the fixup kernel adds the same fp32 values in the same
order as for an f32 dst and rounds the sum once. With an f32 dst nothing changes.

